n, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}↔{R}_{4}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -2\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+(-2){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -12\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=5 \\\\ 3{x}_{2} &=9 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=3 \\\\ -4{x}_{2} &=-12.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second,  third and fourth equations, we get ${x}_{2}=3.$ From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3 & =5 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $[A]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nFinally, $2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=2\\cdot 2+3=7.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186496649 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186497431 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496649 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186497463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496649 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186497470 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496649 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186497483 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496649 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186497489 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496649 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496649 #edb/ref 1045 "The Coordinates of a Vector Relative to a Basis in Abstract Vector Spaces" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496649 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186497483 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496649 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046659 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496649 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048333 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496649 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "7a5a6986-cd36-531a-9f9c-dcfb6003f956" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496666 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496666 #edb/