 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497380 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following matrices:\n\n$$\n{B}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 6 \\\\ 9 & 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,{B}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 8\\end{bmatrix},\\,A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 \\\\ -7 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nIf $B=\\{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}\\},$ and $[A]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},$ then ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186497380 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8b164922-7a86-5e35-904e-baea511723b4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497380 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{B}_{1}+{x}_{2}{B}_{2}=A.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 6 \\\\ 9 & 7\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 8\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 \\\\ -7 & 9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} & 6{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2} \\\\ 9{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} & 7{x}_{1}+8{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 \\\\ -7 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} &=2 \\\\ 6{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2} &=4 \\\\ 9{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=-7 \\\\ 7{x}_{1}+8{x}_{2} &=9.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 9 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 7 & 8 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 9 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 7 & 8 & 9\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & \\begin{bmatrix}6 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 9 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 7 & 8 & 9\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{3}{2}){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+(-\\frac{7}{6}){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & \\begin{bmatrix}6 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{13}{2} & -13 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{13}{6} & \\frac{13}{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}6{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2} &=4 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=2 \\\\ -\\frac{13}{2}{x}_{2} &=-13 \\\\ \\frac{13}{6}{x}_{2} &=\\frac{13}{3}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second, third and fourth equations, we get ${x}_{2}=2.$ From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}_{1}+5\\cdot 2 & =4 \\\\ 6{x}_{1} & =-6 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $[A]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-1+2=1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186497431 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186497489 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497431 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "336b9f6a-688f-5c80-8b64-72381caefc8e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497431 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186366587 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497463 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186497431 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497463 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a74c6d5d-0020-5707-b38c-10b2bc08bb70" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497463 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186360539 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497470 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "bb742e8c-2853-5793-a821-ef78c316058a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497470 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186243954 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497483 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186497463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497483 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "eefaff6d-e472-53e9-a5c9-55ede9a20c93" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497483 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186497380 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497489 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186497470 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497489 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "fe154e6d-10aa-5895-a8de-82e02aff4a99" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497489 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186360542 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559100 #edb/ref 1080 "p(t)=-3t+2{t}^{2}-2{t}^{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559100 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/