/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559788 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2ade0c9c-871d-5f78-8adc-bcd701d0727a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559788 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{B}_{1}+{x}_{2}{B}_{2}=A.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-10 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} & 2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ 0 & 3{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-10 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 10\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-10 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -10 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 10\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -10 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 10\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -20 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -20\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-10 \\\\ 5{x}_{2}=-20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second  equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-4.$ From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+2(-4) & =-10 \\\\ -{x}_{1} & =-2 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=2+(-4)=-2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559815 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186559679 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559815 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95007" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559815 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559815 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the polynomials ${p}_{1}(t)$ and ${p}_{2}(t),$ given by\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=t-{t}^{3},\\,{p}_{2}(t)=2{t}^{2}+5{t}^{3}.\n$$\n\nFind $p(t)$ given that $B=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{1},{p}_{2}\\},$ and the coordinates of $p(t)$ relative to $B$ are $[p(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559815 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "71981b01-d421-5e25-8cb2-44a17e6d5470" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559815 #edb/ref 1074 "Any vector in  $\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{1},{p}_{2}\\}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n[p(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(t) & =(-3)\\cdot (t-{t}^{3})+1\\cdot (2{t}^{2}+5{t}^{3}) \\\\  & =-3t+3{t}^{3}+2{t}^{2}+5{t}^{3} \\\\  & =-3t+2{t}^{2}+8{t}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559870 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186559688 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559870 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95014" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559870 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559870 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following matrices:\n\n$$\n{B}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{B}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 12\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIf $B=\\{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}\\},$ and $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559870 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "df9025d6-fcec-59a9-b2fb-091fd502413d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559870 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{B}_{1}+{x}_{2}{B}_{2}=A.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} & -2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ 0 & 3{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 12\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-2 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-6 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 12\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 12\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -10 \\\\ 0 & -9 & 18\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-2 \\\\ 5{x}_{2}=-10 \\\\ -9{x}_{2}=18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third equations, we get ${x}_{2}=-2.$ From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2(-2) & =-2 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=2+(-2)=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559880 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186559670 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559880 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95010" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559880 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559880 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n{A}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{A}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}9 & 4 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. Find the matrix $C$ given that $B=\\{{A}_{1},{A}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{A}_{1},{A}_{2}\\},$ and the coordinates of the matrix $C$ relative to $B$ are $[C]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559880 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ee947d80-6aa8-5dc4-9785-d937ced374de" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559880 #edb/ref 1074 "Any vector in $\\text{Span}\\{{A}_{1},{A}_{2}\\}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{A}_{1}+{x}_{2}{A}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n[C]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =4\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]+(-1)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}9 & 4 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 12\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-9 & -4 \\\\ 5 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -8 \\\\ 5 & 9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
